TITLE:: RCPbindProxy
summary:: The ordered keys of a beat, an RCKeyProxy each, behind one EventPatternProxy
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCKeyProxy, Classes/RCBeat, Classes/PbindProxy

DESCRIPTION::
What code::PbindProxy:: is to code::Pbind::, with an link::Classes/RCKeyProxy:: per key instead of a code::PatternProxy::. The pairs feed a code::Pbind:: held by an code::EventPatternProxy::, so that adding or removing a key swaps the whole pattern on the proxy's quant (nil: at the next event) while editing an existing key is the key's own business (link::Classes/RCKeyProxy#-setSource::). Every add or remove rebuilds the Pbind once and keeps code::finishKey:: last.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: pairs
code::[key, RCKeyProxy, key, RCKeyProxy, ...]::.
argument:: finishKey
The key kept last (link::Classes/RCBeat::'s code::\rc_finish::).
argument:: clock
argument:: quant
The quant of the whole-pattern swaps.

